## What this predicate means

**A `next-by-date` B** — A and B are occurrents (logs / sessions / commits / authorization events / plan transitions) where A's temporal position precedes B's; the assertion points forward in time.  The **pairwise cons-list primitive** for append-only event sequences.  Dagger pair with `previous-by-date`.  Strictly superior to SKOS OrderedCollection for immutable append-only sequences because insertion is O(1) local edit (just add forward and backward pointers at the new node), not O(n) reshuffle of a central list.

