## Formal signature

`{{predicate-name}} : {{domain}} × {{range}} → Bool`

## Characteristics

- **Asymmetric** — A next-by-date B doesn't imply B next-by-date A (OWL 2 RL `prp-asyp`)
- **Irreflexive** — an occurrent doesn't follow itself (OWL 2 RL `prp-irp`)
- **NOT transitive** — A next-by-date B + B next-by-date C does NOT give A next-by-date C.  Chains are walked explicitly (path queries), not collapsed into transitive closure.  This is the pairwise-cons-list property.

## When to use next-by-date

Use `next-by-date` whenever you have a chronologically-ordered sequence of occurrent memorials and need:

- Forward navigation through the chain
- O(1) insertion at any position
- Audit-friendly chain integrity (each link is a single typed-edge)

Examples: session log sequences, commit history projection, authorization event chains, plan-stage transitions, memoir series.

