## Pairwise-cons-list invariant

For any chain `A → B → C → D`:
- Forward: `A next-by-date B`, `B next-by-date C`, `C next-by-date D` (three links; one per node)
- Backward: `D previous-by-date C`, etc. (derived via prp-inv1/inv2 if `:dt/inverse-of` declared)

The chain's integrity is purely local — no central list to maintain.

